1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:10,403
As a statistics PhD student, my day moves between research, coursework,
teaching, and everything around them.

2
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:19,516
There are papers to read, questions to discuss with my advisor, classes to take,
and TA work to prepare.

3
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:24,865
Travel plans and everyday life also need attention.

4
00:00:25,767 --> 00:00:30,602
The challenge is keeping enough context to return to each piece of work.

5
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:37,150
RUWithMe brings those parts of my day into one place.

6
00:00:39,233 --> 00:00:45,251
Research gives each project a home for its current state, materials, and next steps.

7
00:00:46,167 --> 00:00:52,706
Here, Pareto Frontier connects the project overview to its paper and research
notes.

8
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:58,201
Courses keeps coursework and TA responsibilities together.

9
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:02,974
Learn is for topics and skills I want to develop.

10
00:01:03,867 --> 00:01:10,941
Admin and Personal give practical responsibilities a place alongside academic
work.

11
00:01:13,033 --> 00:01:16,677
Today is where I decide what to move forward now.

12
00:01:17,567 --> 00:01:22,890
I can choose a concrete task instead of facing every project at once.

13
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:28,591
The linked project helps me recover the context behind that task.

14
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:35,166
After working, I can record a session with progress, questions, and a next step.

15
00:01:37,267 --> 00:01:42,040
Track brings together saved plans, work sessions, and reviews.

16
00:01:42,933 --> 00:01:47,406
It helps me look back at what happened and prepare a weekly review.

17
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:53,539
Inbox gives a quick idea or an unfinished question somewhere to land.

18
00:01:54,433 --> 00:01:58,137
I can return later and decide where it belongs.

19
00:02:00,233 --> 00:02:04,441
The workspace is stored as local files on my computer.

20
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:09,177
Projects follow a structure I can inspect and change.

21
00:02:10,067 --> 00:02:14,741
Daily gives me a place to think through my work with connected AI.

22
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:19,592
It can suggest a plan or help clarify a next step.

23
00:02:20,467 --> 00:02:24,174
I choose the actions and confirm what gets saved.

24
00:02:25,033 --> 00:02:31,863
With AI assistance, I can also adapt the organization and interface as my needs
change.

25
00:02:33,933 --> 00:02:39,228
This is still an early prototype, built around a personal way of working.

26
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:45,051
The direction is a workspace each researcher can shape for themselves.

27
00:02:45,933 --> 00:02:50,493
Next, let me show how I would use this demo during a research day.
